thing from shipping features and discovering leads to writing and distributing content. With Cofounder, you can build a company as a solo founder.\n\nWe built it around three main beliefs.\n\n1. Starting a company should be easier. You should be able to go from idea to a functioning company in a single day, without getting stuck in the infrastructure, tooling, and setup decisions that have nothing to do with your actual business.\n\n2. Starting a company should be fun. We want running a company to feel like playing a video game, not grinding through operational overhead.\n\n3. Starting a company should make your life better. When your agents are handling the work of a full team, you get to spend your time on what actually matters to you outside of work.\n\nAbout a year ago, I wrote about the concept of superoptimizers â€” agents that manage other agents. I wrote that piece because I had begun to notice a trend: vertical agents were flooding the market.\n\nFrom code gen, to infrastructure, to sales sequencing, there is now a mature well-built vertical agent in every category. If youâ€™re setting up an agent native company, you will want to use these instead of hiring people!\n\nBut thereâ€™s a problem. Thereâ€™s too many of them. They donâ€™t work together. You need a different agent who can coordinate work between all of these various other siloes of agents.\n\nWe have built Cofounder into a superoptimizer (that is, a manager agent) that delegates work across four departments: engineering, sales, marketing, and design. Across all of these departments, we believe it is now possible to run an entire company on Cofounder 2.\n\nUsing Cofounder 2, you can:\n\nGo from idea to live product with fully automated infra, code, and deployment\n\nShip faster with AI agents that write, review, and merge code autonomously\n\nMonetize instantly with Stripe setup and in-app domain purchasing\n\nGrow distribution with AI-generated, optimized, and auto-scheduled marketing\n\nDiscover 